{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"db502bca-7b44-4288-9b5f-39e8066ddf8a","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":36,"previousEventHash":"sha256:46fcf9f1e92e4953147bc03d046feba96978b0d4cb0fde5fd0053d9f97d76ce5","type":"reviewer.artifact-published","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0381c-afc9-7589-8854-899e1a2ee2b3","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-25T09:33:07.916Z","idempotencyKey":"node:review-correctness-1:artifact-published","payload":{"nodeId":"review-correctness-1","node":"review-correctness","attempt":1,"round":1,"headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","baseSha":"86fff740db2e1ab31fc651fc80ea00ec7c5bdcbd","publishedCommentId":5408402068,"reviewerResult":{"schema":"forgedock.reviewer-result/v1","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","verdict":"findings","findings":[{"id":"CORRECTNESS-ORCH-LIFECYCLE-RECEIPT","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":1840,"summary":"The orchestration lane pins the resolve child receipt, but each bounded node replaces link.subagentRunId, so later lifecycle events are rejected as stale.","evidence":["The orchestration lane stores the receipt returned by startIssue in lane.started, while #dispatchNode assigns link.subagentRunId = receipt.runId for every non-reviewer node at work-on.ts:1840; reviewer launches leave a launch sentinel because the assignment is inside the !reviewerNode branch.","The ready/completed parent path emits link.subagentRunId at work-on.ts:1565, which is therefore a later node receipt (or reviewer sentinel), not the receipt stored in the lane.","orchestrate.ts:355 returns whenever event.subagentRunId differs from lane.subagentRunId. After prepare-pr/review this differs deterministically, so lane.ready, lane.failed, and lane.completed events are ignored and orchestration cannot integrate or finish the issue."]},{"id":"CORRECTNESS-IMPLEMENT-CONTEXT","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":1066,"summary":"Fresh bounded implementation nodes receive only a generic handoff instead of the issue and plan, so they cannot reliably implement the requested behavior.","evidence":["startIssue builds the issue title/body/labels JSON once for resolve, but after every node #reconcileNode dispatches the next node with the literal 'Resume from durable node artifacts only.' at work-on.ts:1066.","SubagentsRpcClient forwards that value as the bounded task's issueContext at subagents.ts:266; no issue or plan artifact is included in the ActiveRunLink or launch input.","The bounded task forbids bash for implement at subagents.ts:263, child-runtime blocks bash outside resolve/investigate/plan at child-runtime.ts:171-179, and allowedNodeTools('implement') exposes only forge_diff/forge_commit/forge_finalize_node at child-runtime.ts:1054. The fresh implement worker has no issue/GitHub/state access; remediation additionally only says to read inaccessible durable artifacts at work-on.ts:1787-1788."]},{"id":"CORRECTNESS-PARENT-NODE-RESTART","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":238,"summary":"Controller restart cannot reconcile a parent-owned node because attach only resumes active child receipts and never dispatches currentNodeId parent work.","evidence":["#dispatchNode routes review-join, ci, decision, merge, close, and cleanup directly into #runParentNode while persisting currentNodeId, with no activeNodes entry (work-on.ts:1662-1666).","On attach, the recovery loop at work-on.ts:238-266 handles only activeNodes; when that map is empty it checks a launch sentinel or calls rpc.status and waits for a legacy ForgeWorkOnResult (work-on.ts:267-279). It never checks parentNodeFromId/currentNodeId or calls #runParentNode.","A crash during a parent operation therefore leaves its durable node running and the restored link unable to progress; for a standalone run the lease also remains held despite no resumable provider child."]},{"id":"CORRECTNESS-REMEDIATION-OLD-DECISION","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":2080,"summary":"Integration selects the first completed decision rather than the latest awaiting-merge decision, so a successful remediation round cannot merge.","evidence":["The decision node deliberately records outcome remediation-required when fixable findings remain and another review round is allowed (work-on.ts:1422-1424), after which dispatcher creates a later decision node.","integrateIssue uses Object.values(current.state.nodes).find(...) at work-on.ts:2080. Object insertion order places decision-1 before decision-2, so after round two is approved it selects the old remediation-required decision.","The next line rejects that result unless outcome is awaiting-merge, causing orchestration integration to throw and the lane to be marked failed even though the latest review passed."]},{"id":"CORRECTNESS-REVIEWER-ID-ALIAS","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"medium","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":1649,"summary":"Short reviewer aliases accepted by the finalizer are not normalized before the review gate, causing a false incomplete-panel block.","evidence":["forge_finalize_reviewer explicitly accepts either 'security' or 'forge-review-security' (and the correctness equivalents) at child-runtime.ts:689-696; #loadReviewerResult accepts the same aliases at work-on.ts:1088-1095.","#aggregateFromState copies reviewer.reviewer verbatim into completedReviewers at work-on.ts:1649.","The configured policy requires full names ('forge-review-correctness' and 'forge-review-security'), and evaluateReviewGate compares completedReviewers literally. A valid result using reviewer:'security' is consequently treated as a missing required reviewer and cannot merge."]},{"id":"CORRECTNESS-WORKFLOW-LABELS","reviewer":"forge-review-correctness","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"medium","category":"correctness","file":"src/workflows/work-on.ts","line":1560,"summary":"The bounded parent dispatcher never advances workflow labels after starting/reviewing, leaving completed or invalid issues misclassified.","evidence":["The new start path sets only workflow:investigating at work-on.ts:596; bounded artifact reconciliation posts comments at work-on.ts:867 without setting a workflow label.","forge_prepare_review sets workflow:in-review in child-runtime.ts:647, but the parent decision/merge/close/cleanup path at work-on.ts:1560-1584 only posts artifacts and node events; it never sets workflow:awaiting-merge, workflow:merged, workflow:invalid, or workflow:decomposed.","The only workflow:merged call is in the legacy #finalize path at work-on.ts:2732-2735, which the bounded node dispatcher does not invoke, so normal bounded runs leave GitHub issue labels stale."]}],"filesReviewed":["src/workflows/work-on.ts","src/workflows/orchestrate.ts","src/adapters/subagents.ts","src/agents/child-runtime.ts","src/core/dispatcher.ts","src/core/review.ts","src/core/orchestration.ts","src/adapters/github-projection.ts","test/core/reviewer-lifecycle.test.ts","test/workflows/work-on.test.ts","test/adapters/subagents.test.ts"],"limitations":["Tests and typecheck were not executed in this read-only review; findings are based on static inspection of the frozen worktree and its tests."]},"evidence":["pr:31","comment:5408402068"]}}
{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"b1b385c9-1d11-4193-af8f-cbf8197afc7e","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":37,"previousEventHash":"sha256:08b13c1ff2b3df77714d45faf9c94bc04a0353604fd7740c516b773515aa8b0f","type":"reviewer.artifact-published","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a0381c-afc9-7589-8854-899e1a2ee2b3","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-25T09:33:40.878Z","idempotencyKey":"node:review-security-1:artifact-published","payload":{"nodeId":"review-security-1","node":"review-security","attempt":1,"round":1,"headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","baseSha":"86fff740db2e1ab31fc651fc80ea00ec7c5bdcbd","publishedCommentId":5408410243,"reviewerResult":{"schema":"forgedock.reviewer-result/v1","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","reviewer":"security","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","verdict":"findings","findings":[{"id":"SECURITY-001","reviewer":"security","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"critical","category":"security","file":"src/agents/child-runtime.ts","line":171,"summary":"Read-only nodes can execute unrestricted bash with the parent environment.","evidence":["The tool_call hook returns immediately for bash on resolve, investigate, and plan nodes; it does not inspect or allowlist the command (lines 171-181).","FORGE_WORK_ON_TOOLS exposes bash to every bounded writer node (src/agents/register.ts:20-24), so the hook is the only command boundary.","The native bash path is not run through safeEnvironment; a prompt-injected issue can invoke gh/git/curl, read user files or GitHub CLI credentials, and perform GitHub writes or pushes despite the read-only node contract."]},{"id":"SECURITY-002","reviewer":"security","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"security","file":"src/agents/child-runtime.ts","line":187,"summary":"The child guard does not make resolve/investigate/plan read-only: write and edit are permitted on any in-worktree path.","evidence":["After the Forge-tool check, the hook handles read/write/edit/grep/find/ls only by checking path containment and then returns; there is no node-based denial for write or edit (lines 187-204).","The same FORGE_WORK_ON_TOOLS list gives write and edit to every bounded node (src/agents/register.ts:20-29).","A resolve or investigate child can therefore modify source, workflow, or policy files before implementation; later forge_commit stages every changed path via git add -A -- ...changedPaths (child-runtime.ts:410-422), with no accepted-plan allowlist or clean-boundary check."]},{"id":"SECURITY-003","reviewer":"security","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"data-loss","file":"src/agents/materialize.ts","line":100,"summary":"Agent materialization follows repository-controlled symlinks and can overwrite files outside the Forge runtime directory.","evidence":["materializeForgeAgents is called on the freshly checked-out worktree before the child starts (src/workflows/work-on.ts:555).","The implementation creates .pi/agents with mkdir but never rejects symlink components, then writes fixed agent filenames with writeFile; writeFile follows a tracked symlink at .pi/agents/forge-work-on.md (materialize.ts:25-27, 97-101).","A repository can commit that path as a symlink to another tracked file, an external writable path, or a host configuration file; the write occurs as the user and can corrupt source/policy data or overwrite an outside file before any child path guard runs."]},{"id":"SECURITY-004","reviewer":"security","runId":"e3f125e3-2c3a-4c51-9a8c-e3254418ad9a","headSha":"8aee96d4b8e41e0ec28edcf47e52c23ef060f360","confidence":"confirmed","severity":"high","category":"auth","file":"src/ui/commands.ts","line":50,"summary":"The model-callable forge_orchestrate tool has no enforced user confirmation and always authorizes expired-lease takeover.","evidence":["The tool description asks the LLM to resolve and confirm, but execute ignores sourceExpression and resolutionSummary and unconditionally calls orchestrator.start with allowExpiredTakeover: true (commands.ts:27-50).","orchestrate.start uses that boolean to cancel the expired orchestration and release its lease without an authorization identity (workflows/orchestrate.ts:158-174); the only confirmation requirement is prompt text.","An indirect prompt injection in GitHub issue text, or any direct model tool call, can dispatch arbitrary positive issue numbers and cancel a prior orchestration; with auto-merge policy this can launch writes/merges without the promised operator approval."]}],"filesReviewed":["src/agents/child-runtime.ts","src/agents/materialize.ts","src/agents/register.ts","src/ui/commands.ts","src/workflows/orchestrate.ts","src/workflows/work-on.ts","src/adapters/subagents.ts","src/adapters/git.ts","src/core/lease.ts","src/core/policy.ts","SECURITY.md","DESIGN.md"],"limitations":["Static review of the frozen worktree; no live GitHub or provider execution was performed.","No comparison against an unfrozen base checkout was used."]},"evidence":["pr:31","comment:5408410243"]}}
